{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LFxR3CSBZBtoQgUYcZNJoH","type":"tool_result","content":"diff --git a/.pose/specs/2026-11-26-pose-validate-read-only-index-followups.md b/.pose/specs/2026-11-26-pose-validate-read-only-index-followups.md\nindex 5cfc0c68..bf6d54a7 100644\n--- a/.pose/specs/2026-11-26-pose-validate-read-only-index-followups.md\n+++ b/.pose/specs/2026-11-26-pose-validate-read-only-index-followups.md\n@@ -61,6 +61,8 @@ Records and indexes written by earlier engines keep their meaning.\n - created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_index_open_unix.go\n - created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_index_open_other.go\n - modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads_test.go\n+- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads_linux_test.go\n+- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_attempt_ledger.go\n - modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/check.go\n - modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go\n - modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/report.go\n@@ -103,6 +105,10 @@ The split-index touch is Git's own: measured with `core.splitIndex=true`, a plai\n - Basis: R1\n The index is judged on the file actually opened, opened with `O_NONBLOCK` where FIFOs exist, instead of a stat before the open: a stat-then-open pair refuses an index replaced atomically in between (round 5, N22), and opening without blocking keeps a FIFO from hanging the read (round 4, N21).\n \n+### Decision D3\n+- Basis: R2\n+The index lookup runs under the caller's context where the caller has one (`ReadOnlyIndexContext`, used by the review history reader within its 30 s), and under a 30 s bound of its own otherwise. Git's standard error is kept, and a failure in which Git names the index is marked `ErrIndexUnreadable`; the read-only command runs with `LC_ALL=C` so that holds in any locale.\n+\n ## 6. Validation\n \n ### Strategy\n@@ -115,15 +121,16 @@ Each requirement gets a regression test shown failing before its code.\n \n ### Execution log\n - 2026-11-26: R1 opens without blocking and judges the opened file; R2 reports a failed index read in `check`, names it in scope selection (`ErrIndexUnreadable`) and warns in `report`; R3 locates the index with `--git-path` relative to the root, within a 30 s deadline; R4 falls back to the private copy when the memory file or its time cannot be set. Each has a test that fails with its guard mutated out: `TestReadOnlyIndexToleratesAnAtomicallyReplacedIndex`, `TestAFailedIndexReadIsReported`, `TestReadOnlyIndexFindsTheIndexFromASubdirectory`, `TestThePrivateIndexCopyLeavesTheIndexAlone`. R6 adds `TestReadOnlyIndexDiffCoversConflictsRangesAndDirtySubmodules`, which passes on the existing reader. R5 is L1 (D1).\n+- 2026-11-26: review round 1 (rrn-4262ae59adfc1641) requested changes. N1–N2: a corrupt index, which Git itself refuses, is now reported with Git's own message and marked as an index failure in check, scope selection and report (`TestACorruptIndexIsReportedWithItsCause`; fails with the classification or check's capture removed). N3: D3. N4: the memfd and timestamp calls are replaceable, and `TestReadOnlyIndexFallsBackWithoutAMemoryFile` fails with either fallback removed. N5: the R6 test makes the stat cache stale before every read, so it fails with the protection or the ledger's use of it removed, and the CLI concurrency test runs `ReviewRunHistoryFindings`. N8: failures handing the index to Git are index failures, and a failing memfd write falls back too. N9: the report states that the list could not be read, and a plain `pose report` outside a repository stays silent. N10: the check's findings are localised. N6, N7 and N11 are follow-ups.\n \n ### Results summary\n The full `pose-mcp` suite passes; the canonical result is refreshed with `pose validate --carry`.\n \n ### Requirement trace\n - R1 [satisfied] test:TestReadOnlyIndexToleratesAnAtomicallyReplacedIndex, test:TestReadOnlyIndexRefusesAFIFOIndex\n-- R2 [satisfied] test:TestAFailedIndexReadIsReported\n+- R2 [satisfied] test:TestAFailedIndexReadIsReported, test:TestACorruptIndexIsReportedWithItsCause\n - R3 [satisfied] test:TestReadOnlyIndexFindsTheIndexFromASubdirectory\n-- R4 [satisfied] test:TestThePrivateIndexCopyLeavesTheIndexAlone\n+- R4 [satisfied] test:TestThePrivateIndexCopyLeavesTheIndexAlone, test:TestReadOnlyIndexFallsBackWithoutAMemoryFile\n - R5 [satisfied] (accepted limit L1, decision D1)\n - R6 [satisfied] test:TestReadOnlyIndexDiffCoversConflictsRangesAndDirtySubmodules\n \n@@ -145,4 +152,7 @@ The read-only index read tolerates an atomically replaced index, reports its fai\n L1 above.\n \n ### Follow-ups\n-None. Origin: `pose-validate-reads-leave-the-index-alone` (done 2026-11-26).\n+Origin: `pose-validate-reads-leave-the-index-alone` (done 2026-11-26).\n+- [open] Test the index lookup against a Git that echoes an unknown `--path-format` (a stand-in executable), so restoring the flag fails a test (review round 1, N6). (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-12-26)\n+- [open] Test the `pose report` warning for an unreadable change list end to end (review round 1, N7). (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-12-26)\n+- [open] List the changed specs of a POSE root below the repository top: `git diff --name-only` names top-relative paths that the `.pose/specs/` filter drops, so their ready transitions go unchecked (review round 1, N11; pre-existing). (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:medium review:2026-12-26)\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/check.go b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/check.go\nindex 91093c98..b0901556 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/check.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/check.go\n@@ -1,6 +1,7 @@\n package cli\n \n import (\n+\t\"bytes\"\n \t\"context\"\n \t\"encoding/json\"\n \t\"fmt\"\n@@ -1141,14 +1142,17 @@ func (checker *nativeChecker) readyTransitionCandidates() []string {\n \t\t\t\tdone()\n \t\t\t\t// The specs this read would name go unchecked: say so\n \t\t\t\t// (review round 5, N23).\n-\t\t\t\tchecker.failOrWarn(fmt.Sprintf(\"ready transitions: the changed specs cannot be listed: %v\", err))\n+\t\t\t\tchecker.failOrWarn(checker.message(fmt.Sprintf(\"ready transitions: the changed specs cannot be listed: %v\", err), fmt.Sprintf(\"transições de prontidão: as specs alteradas não podem ser listadas: %v\", err)))\n \t\t\t\tcontinue\n \t\t\t}\n \t\t}\n+\t\tvar stderr bytes.Buffer\n+\t\tcmd.Stderr = &stderr\n \t\toutput, err := cmd.Output()\n \t\tdone()\n \t\tif err != nil {\n-\t\t\tchecker.failOrWarn(fmt.Sprintf(\"ready transitions: git %s failed: %v\", command[0], err))\n+\t\t\terr = pose.GitReadError(\"git \"+command[0], err, stderr.Bytes())\n+\t\t\tchecker.failOrWarn(checker.message(fmt.Sprintf(\"ready transitions: the changed specs cannot be listed: %v\", err), fmt.Sprintf(\"transições de prontidão: as specs alteradas não podem ser listadas: %v\", err)))\n \t\t\tcontinue\n \t\t}\n \t\tfor _, rel := range strings.Fields(string(output)) {\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/report.go b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/report.go\nindex fd5e2d2f..27ca9c3c 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/report.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/report.go\n@@ -6,6 +6,7 @@ import (\n \t\"crypto/sha256\"\n \t\"encoding/hex\"\n \t\"encoding/json\"\n+\t\"errors\"\n \t\"fmt\"\n \t\"github.com/harne8/pose-mcp/internal/cli/cliout\"\n \t\"io\"\n@@ -197,7 +198,13 @@ func runReportWith(root string, args []string, validationLog []byte, summary *va\n \t\t}\n \t}\n \tfilesChanged, err := reportChangedFiles(root, values[\"since\"])\n+\tif err != nil && values[\"since\"] == \"\" && !errors.Is(err, posemodel.ErrIndexUnreadable) {\n+\t\t// Outside a repository the plain listing stays silent, as before\n+\t\t// (review round 1, N9).\n+\t\terr = nil\n+\t}\n \tif err != nil {\n+\t\tfilesChanged = []string{cliText(locale, \"_The changed files could not be listed: \", \"_Os arquivos alterados não puderam ser listados: \") + err.Error() + \"_\"}\n \t\t// The report still writes, without the list it could not read\n \t\t// (review round 5, N23).\n \t\trender(stderr, stderr).Finding(cliout.Finding{State: cliout.StateWarning, Code: \"report-changed-files\", Message: fmt.Sprintf(cliText(locale, \"the changed files cannot be listed: %v\", \"os arquivos alterados não podem ser listados: %v\"), err)})\n@@ -311,7 +318,12 @@ func reportChangedFiles(root, since string) ([]string, error) {\n \tif since != \"\" {\n \t\toutput, err = posemodel.RawGitDiffReadOnly(root, args...)\n \t} else {\n-\t\toutput, err = posemodel.RawGit(args...).Output()\n+\t\tvar stderr bytes.Buffer\n+\t\tcmd := posemodel.RawGit(args...)\n+\t\tcmd.Stderr = &stderr\n+\t\tif output, err = cmd.Output(); err != nil {\n+\t\t\terr = posemodel.GitReadError(\"git status\", err, stderr.Bytes())\n+\t\t}\n \t}\n \tif err != nil {\n \t\treturn nil, err\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_reads_index_test.go b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_reads_index_test.go\nindex 75eeaa0a..8131857d 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_reads_index_test.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_reads_index_test.go\n@@ -2,6 +2,7 @@ package cli\n \n import (\n \t\"bytes\"\n+\tposemodel \"github.com/harne8/pose-mcp/internal/pose\"\n \t\"os\"\n \t\"os/exec\"\n \t\"path/filepath\"\n@@ -90,6 +91,9 @@ func TestConcurrentValidationReadsNeverChangeTheIndex(t *testing.T) {\n \t\t\t\t_, _ = computeChangedScopeWith(root, \"HEAD\", \"\", nil, scopeMetadata{})\n \t\t\t\t_, _ = reportChangedFiles(root, \"HEAD\")\n \t\t\t\t(&nativeChecker{root: root}).readyTransitionCandidates()\n+\t\t\t\t// The review history reader runs concurrently too (review\n+\t\t\t\t// round 1, N5).\n+\t\t\t\t_, _ = posemodel.Store{Root: root}.ReviewRunHistoryFindings()\n \t\t\t}\n \t\t}()\n \t}\n@@ -173,3 +177,26 @@ func TestAFailedIndexReadIsReported(t *testing.T) {\n \t\tt.Fatal(\"report hid a failed index read\")\n \t}\n }\n+\n+// Review round 1, N1–N2 of spec pose-validate-read-only-index-followups: a\n+// corrupt index, which git itself refuses, is reported as an index failure\n+// with what git said, not as an unknown revision.\n+func TestACorruptIndexIsReportedWithItsCause(t *testing.T) {\n+\troot, _ := staleIndexRepo(t)\n+\tif err := os.WriteFile(filepath.Join(root, \".git\", \"index\"), []byte(\"not an index at all\"), 0o644); err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t}\n+\tvar out bytes.Buffer\n+\tchecker := &nativeChecker{root: root, mode: \"strict\", locale: localeEN, stdout: &out}\n+\tchecker.readyTransitionCandidates()\n+\tif checker.errors == 0 || !strings.Contains(out.String(), \"index\") {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"the check did not name the corrupt index: %d %s\", checker.errors, out.String())\n+\t}\n+\t_, err := computeChangedScopeWith(root, \"HEAD\", \"\", nil, scopeMetadata{})\n+\tif err == nil || strings.Contains(err.Error(), \"revision unknown?\") || !strings.Contains(err.Error(), \"index\") {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"scope selection mislabelled a corrupt index: %v\", err)\n+\t}\n+\tif _, err := reportChangedFiles(root, \"HEAD\"); err == nil || !strings.Contains(err.Error(), \"index\") {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"report did not name the corrupt index: %v\", err)\n+\t}\n+}\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads.go b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads.go\nindex 6e145f7f..bffc9bf4 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads.go\n@@ -1,6 +1,7 @@\n package pose\n \n import (\n+\t\"bytes\"\n \t\"context\"\n \t\"errors\"\n \t\"fmt\"\n@@ -36,11 +37,17 @@ const indexLookupTimeout = 30 * time.Second\n // to read root's index without being able to write it. The returned function\n // releases what it holds; call it after the command ends.\n func ReadOnlyIndex(cmd *exec.Cmd, root string) (func(), error) {\n+\tctx, cancel := context.WithTimeout(context.Background(), indexLookupTimeout)\n+\tdefer cancel()\n+\treturn ReadOnlyIndexContext(ctx, cmd, root)\n+}\n+\n+// ReadOnlyIndexContext is ReadOnlyIndex with the lookup of the index bound by\n+// ctx, the caller's deadline (review round 1, N3).\n+func ReadOnlyIndexContext(ctx context.Context, cmd *exec.Cmd, root string) (func(), error) {\n \t// `--git-path` without `--path-format`, which Git before 2.31 would echo\n \t// back as a path that does not exist (review round 5, N26): the answer is\n \t// relative to root unless absolute.\n-\tctx, cancel := context.WithTimeout(context.Background(), indexLookupTimeout)\n-\tdefer cancel()\n \tout, err := gitCommandContext(ctx, \"--no-replace-objects\", \"-C\", root, \"rev-parse\", \"--git-path\", \"index\").Output()\n \tif err != nil {\n \t\treturn func() {}, fmt.Errorf(\"pose: the index of %s cannot be located: %w: %w\", root, ErrIndexUnreadable, err)\n@@ -78,7 +85,29 @@ func ReadOnlyIndex(cmd *exec.Cmd, root string) (func(), error) {\n \t// its stat only when the file is older than the index, so a fresher copy\n \t// would hide a change made in the index's own second (review round 2,\n \t// N10, racy-clean entries).\n-\treturn readOnlyIndexFor(cmd, raw, info.ModTime())\n+\t// Git's messages in English, so GitReadError can tell an index failure\n+\t// whatever the user's locale.\n+\tcmd.Env = append(cmd.Env, \"LC_ALL=C\", \"LANGUAGE=C\")\n+\tdone, err := readOnlyIndexFor(cmd, raw, info.ModTime())\n+\tif err != nil {\n+\t\treturn done, fmt.Errorf(\"pose: the index of %s cannot be handed to git: %w: %w\", root, ErrIndexUnreadable, err)\n+\t}\n+\treturn done, nil\n+}\n+\n+// GitReadError describes a failed git read with what git said on standard\n+// error, marking it ErrIndexUnreadable when git names the index (review\n+// round 1, N1–N2: a corrupt index made git exit 128 with the cause only on\n+// its standard error).\n+func GitReadError(what string, err error, stderr []byte) error {\n+\tsaid := strings.TrimSpace(string(stderr))\n+\tif said == \"\" {\n+\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"%s failed: %w\", what, err)\n+\t}\n+\tif strings.Contains(said, \"index\") {\n+\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"%s failed: %w: %w: %s\", what, ErrIndexUnreadable, err, said)\n+\t}\n+\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"%s failed: %w: %s\", what, err, said)\n }\n \n // privateIndexCopy hands raw to cmd as a private copy: Git refreshes and may\n@@ -113,5 +142,11 @@ func RawGitDiffReadOnly(root string, args ...string) ([]byte, error) {\n \tif err != nil {\n \t\treturn nil, err\n \t}\n-\treturn cmd.Output()\n+\tvar stderr bytes.Buffer\n+\tcmd.Stderr = &stderr\n+\tout, err := cmd.Output()\n+\tif err != nil {\n+\t\treturn nil, GitReadError(\"git diff\", err, stderr.Bytes())\n+\t}\n+\treturn out, nil\n }\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads_linux.go b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads_linux.go\nindex c6c161f2..508b1ec5 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads_linux.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads_linux.go\n@@ -17,7 +17,7 @@ import (\n // exist, so the lock fails for any user, root included, and the refresh is\n // not written. No file is created.\n func readOnlyIndexFor(cmd *exec.Cmd, raw []byte, modTime time.Time) (func(), error) {\n-\tfd, err := unix.MemfdCreate(\"pose-index/none\", unix.MFD_CLOEXEC)\n+\tfd, err := memfdCreate(\"pose-index/none\", unix.MFD_CLOEXEC)\n \tif err != nil {\n \t\t// No memory file here (an old kernel, a seccomp filter): the private\n \t\t// copy keeps the index untouched too (review round 5, N27).\n@@ -26,14 +26,14 @@ func readOnlyIndexFor(cmd *exec.Cmd, raw []byte, modTime time.Time) (func(), err\n \tf := os.NewFile(uintptr(fd), \"pose-index\")\n \tif _, err := f.Write(raw); err != nil {\n \t\tf.Close()\n-\t\treturn func() {}, err\n+\t\treturn privateIndexCopy(cmd, raw, modTime) // review round 1, N8\n \t}\n \tif _, err := f.Seek(0, 0); err != nil {\n \t\tf.Close()\n-\t\treturn func() {}, err\n+\t\treturn privateIndexCopy(cmd, raw, modTime)\n \t}\n \tts := unix.NsecToTimespec(modTime.UnixNano())\n-\tif err := unix.UtimesNanoAt(unix.AT_FDCWD, fmt.Sprintf(\"/proc/self/fd/%d\", fd), []unix.Timespec{ts, ts}, 0); err != nil {\n+\tif err := utimesNanoAt(unix.AT_FDCWD, fmt.Sprintf(\"/proc/self/fd/%d\", fd), []